/**
 * Elfsight floating reviews badge — sitewide.
 *
 * Nothing else competes for the bottom of the viewport any more: the sticky
 * mobile call bar was removed in favour of this, on the reasoning that the
 * header CTA is always on screen and social proof earns the corner. So the
 * badge simply sits where Elfsight puts it and needs no positioning help.
 *
 * If a bottom-anchored element is ever reintroduced, know this before trying to
 * move the badge around it:
 *
 *   - Elfsight has no per-breakpoint position setting. `badgeFloatingPosition`
 *     is a single value, and the bundle discards it below its mobile
 *     breakpoint, hardcoding a bottom-centred position instead:
 *         re ? { position: 'bottom', verticalOffset: 20, horizontalOffset: 0 } : i
 *     `badgeVisibilityOnDevices` lets you show or hide per device, but not
 *     place it differently — which is the setting this actually needed.
 *
 *   - CSS cannot reach it. The widget mounts into attachShadow({mode:'open'}),
 *     and shadow DOM encapsulates styles, so an external stylesheet has no
 *     effect at all regardless of selector.
 *
 *   - Class names are build hashes from styled-components and change between
 *     releases, so they are not a stable hook either.
 *
 * The scripted workaround that injected styles into the shadow root is in git
 * history. It worked in principle but meant reaching into a vendor's shadow DOM
 * on every mutation, which is not worth carrying to avoid a layout decision.
 */
---

